                    <birth when="1719">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1804-09-09"/>
                    <occupation>reformer</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Thomas Brand was the chief benefactor of Thomas Hollis's will and he changed his name in honour of recognition of his generosity. He was elected fellow of the 
      Royal Society in 1756 and of the Society of Antiquaries in 1757. He was a founder member of the Society for Consitutional Information in 1780 and the Revolution Society in 
      1788.</p>
                        <p>Godwin recorded meeting him first in 1784 in the 1796 lists.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 1, fol. 97: 10 January 1791</bibl>
